@.str.3 = private unnamed_addr constant [1016 x i8] c"NearestNeighborSearch class for nearest neighbor search. \0A\0AThis class holds multiple index types to accelerate various nearest neighbor \0Asearch operations for a dataset of points with shape {n,d} with `n` as the number\0Aof points and `d` as the dimension of the points. The class supports knn search,\0Afixed-radius search, multi-radius search, and hybrid search.\0A\0AExample:\0A    The following example demonstrates how to perform knn search using the class::\0A        \0A        import open3d as o3d\0A        import numpy as np\0A\0A        dataset = np.random.rand(10,3)\0A        query_points = np.random.rand(5,3)\0A\0A        nns = o3d.core.nns.NearestNeighborSearch(dataset)\0A\0A        # initialize the knn_index before we can use knn_search\0A        nns.knn_index()\0A\0A        # perform knn search to get the 3 closest points with respect to the \0A        # Euclidean distance. The returned distance is given as the squared\0A        # distances\0A        indices, squared_distances = nns.knn_search(query_points, knn=3)\0A\0A                \00", align 1
